Surface nature:  IMPERATIVE app-global UI primitive. The web source is a module-level pub/sub store
                 (useSyncExternalStore) feeding a portal-rendered menu host; it takes its items as plain
                 data resolved by the caller at right-click time and renders — there is NO fetch, NO
                 React-Query cache, NO Promise. So it has NO loading / error / stale / offline branch
                 (nothing to fetch, fail, age, or disconnect). Reproduced branches = the source's REAL ones:
                 closed (no menu), open with one+ rows (each enabled / disabled / destructive-tinted, with an
                 optional leading icon + trailing shortcut), and the empty item set (web silently refuses to
                 open it; natively a friendly empty body, never a blank box). No loading/error/stale/offline
                 chrome was fabricated — same faithful-parity stance as siblings StickyChipBar(0200),
                 ActiveFilterChips(0147), SortControl(0159). Browser-only facilities map to native peers:
                 useSyncExternalStore store -> @Observable ContextMenuController (app-global .shared, the
                 module-store parity); ContextMenuRoot portal -> ContextMenuOverlay host; useContextMenu hook
                 -> .teslaSyncContextMenu trigger modifier; useLayoutEffect measure-and-flip -> pure
                 ContextMenuProjector.place(); useId/role=menu -> SwiftUI a11y container; right-click ->
                 long-press / secondary press.

Data sources reproduced (from web source):
  • useSyncExternalStore -> ContextMenuController (@Observable @MainActor state-holder, P1/S8)
  • useTranslation       -> ContextMenuStrings facade (P1/S10), table "ContextMenu"
  • useId                -> SwiftUI accessibility container identity (role="menu" peer)
  • useLayoutEffect      -> ContextMenuProjector.place() measure-and-flip (pure, unit-tested)

